<!-- Removes the 52 field configs superseded by the record-type consolidation.

     TEKCO_RecordTypeDeveloperName__c now holds a comma-separated LIST of the record types a
     rule covers, so a field no longer needs one config per population. Each pair
     IndividualP_X + Patient_X becomes one Account_X carrying
     "ACCCO_IndividualPerson,ACCCO_Patient". Coverage is unchanged: a script compared, for each
     (object, field), the union of record types before and the list after, over all 50 pairs.

     TEKCO only. The 21 ALH_* configs belong to the Portugal org and are untouched.

     POST-destructive, so the 26 replacements exist before these disappear:

       sf project deploy start ~-manifest anonymization/manifest/package.xml
           ~-post-destructive-changes anonymization/manifest/destructiveChanges-recordtype-consolidation.xml
           ~-dry-run ~-target-org <alias>
     (replace ~- with double dashes; XML comments cannot contain them)

     BEFORE DEPLOYING, CHECK THAT NO RUN IS IN FLIGHT. A chained run reloads its configs from
     the developer names it holds in serialized state; deleting them mid-chain leaves the run
     with nothing to apply, the bypass raised and the audit log stuck on Running:

       SELECT Id, Status, ApexClass.Name, CreatedDate FROM AsyncApexJob
       WHERE Status IN ('Queued','Processing','Preparing','Holding') AND ApexClass.Name LIKE 'TEKCO_%'

     THE CODE MUST BE DEPLOYED FIRST. A version that reads TEKCO_RecordTypeDeveloperName__c as a
     single name would match nothing against "ACCCO_IndividualPerson,ACCCO_Patient" and would
     silently anonymize no Account field at all.
-->
